---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="privacy · avner"
  description="How avkean's public services handle your data: Translate, search, and pi.sg."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1>privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Your privacy means a lot to me, so I try to collect as little data as possible.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="page-section" id="everything">
    <h2>all services</h2>
    <p>
      There are no accounts, ads, analytics or tracking. Everything runs on my own server in
      Singapore behind{' '}<a href="https://bunny.net/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >Bunny CDN</a
      >, and neither of us keeps access logs for these services, only error logs for a short
      while.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" id="translate">
    <h2>translate</h2>
    <p>
      Your text is encrypted on my server and translated by{' '}<a
        href="https://www.privatemode.ai/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Privatemode</a
      >{' '}on confidential computing hardware, so they can't read it either, and nothing gets
      stored. Your IP is only counted in memory for a minute to stop abuse.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" id="search">
    <h2>search</h2>
    <p>
      Searches and suggestions go out to Google, DuckDuckGo, Brave and Kagi from my server, so they
      never see your IP, and I don't log them. The bot check sets a cookie tied to your IP that
      lasts 7 days, while request counts per IP expire within an hour.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" id="pi">
    <h2>pi.sg</h2>
    <p>
      Pi has no link database, since the address is stored in the link itself. With extra
      compression on, your link is compressed in my server's memory and never saved, and Pi
      doesn't keep any logs.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" id="this-site">
    <h2>this website</h2>
    <p>There are no cookies, tracking or access logs here either.</p>
    <p class="updated">Last updated 29 September 2026</p>
  </section>
</Base>
